      "message": "This makes me suspect that the current SchedTune accounting can be almost completely broken, because it\u0027s based on:\n1) schedtune_exit_task, which should be called from do_exit but it\u0027s not\n2) we bail out in schedtune_dequeue_task when PF_EXITING is set.\n\nI remember there was a race condition on v3.18 because when tasks was exiting they was moved to the root CGroups in the to_exit path.\nHere is the original patch:\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/e7ce26f0c8064d970d49acc1dfb8c24504300008\n\n\nAFAIR, this is not more happening in mainline, thus I would say that it should be safe to:\n1) remove this function\n2) remove all the return when \"if (p-\u003eflags \u0026 PF_EXITING)\" is checked in this file\n\nI have an accouting test we can use to verify that it\u0027s working as expected...",
